    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Do you spend a lot of time on your phone and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "social media",
            "ref": "v-social-media"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? Many kids do. In Denmark, the government is worried about this. They want to ban social media for children under 15. They said phones were taking away kids’ childhood."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Phones are good for talking to friends and family. But social media has bad sides, too. In Denmark, kids aged 9 to 14 spend about three hours a day on screens. Many kids see things that are not good for them. This can make them feel sad or worried. Some have trouble reading or "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "paying attention",
            "ref": "v-pay-attention"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in class."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The new rule would stop children under 15 from using social media. But parents can let their children use it if their kids are 13 or older."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Other countries are acting, too. France, Greece, and Spain want to "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "limit"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " kids’ use of social media. In the U.K., companies must protect kids from bad "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "content",
            "ref": "v-content"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Australia will ban social media for under-16s soon."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
